---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/base';

const lastUpdated = '6 September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="PS LASER — Account Deletion Request"
  description="How to request deletion of your PS Laser account and data, in-app or by email, and exactly what is and isn't covered."
  path="/delete-account"
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Legal" title="Account Deletion Request" />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="last-updated reveal">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div class="prose reveal">
        <h2>Option 1 — In the app</h2>
        <p>
          Open the PS LASER app and go to <strong>Settings → Request Account Deletion</strong>.
          Confirming this immediately deactivates your account — you will no longer be able to
          log in — and submits a deletion request for your company's Owner or Manager to review
          and complete.
        </p>

        <h2>Option 2 — By email</h2>
        <p>
          If you can't access the app, email <a href="mailto:pslaser24@gmail.com?subject=Account%20Deletion%20Request">pslaser24@gmail.com</a>
          from the email address associated with your account (or include your registered name
          and employer) with the subject "Account Deletion Request." We'll confirm your
          identity with your company's Owner or Manager and process the request from there.
        </p>

        <h2>What deletion covers</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Your employee profile (name, role, department, shift)</li>
          <li>Your login credentials (PIN hash, security-question answer)</li>
          <li>Device push-notification tokens registered to your account</li>
          <li>Your AI assistant chat history</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What is retained regardless of a deletion request</h2>
        <p>
          Orders, client records, and production/financial history you were involved in are
          kept as business and legal/financial records, the same way they're retained for every
          account — not specific to you. This is existing, standard practice for a
          manufacturing business's bookkeeping and audit trail, described further in our
          <a href={withBase('/privacy')}>Privacy Policy</a>. Your name may continue to appear on historical
          records (for example, "order taken by") even after your account itself is deleted.
        </p>

        <h2>Timeline</h2>
        <p>
          Deactivation (Option 1) is immediate — your account stops working the moment you
          confirm it in the app. Finalizing the deletion request itself is completed by your
          company's Owner or Manager, not automatically, so exact timing after that point can
          vary. For an email request (Option 2), we aim to process it within a reasonable time
          after confirming your identity, and will confirm with you directly once it's received.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .section {
    padding-block: clamp(32px, 6vh, 64px) var(--section-gap);
  }
</style>
